![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Bug](https://img.shields.io/badge/Bug-B71C1C) ![high](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-high-6B6B92)


**Tail operator/connector checks ignore `reference`, so inherited cuts are still flagged**

Inherited cuts still return `truncated`, so `agent-review.stage.ts` clears `improvedCode` and raises the bad-fix notice for the common comma-ended shape. Compute the `reference` stripped tail next to `nonLiteralOf(reference)` and skip the operator and return/connector tail checks when it ends with the same operator, comma, or dangling connector.



<details>
<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>

````text
File libs/code-review/infrastructure/agents/engine/is-usable-fix.ts, lines 339-345:

Tail operator/connector checks ignore `reference`, so inherited cuts are still flagged

The newly threaded `reference` is consulted only by the bracket scan — the operator tail test at line 294 and the return/connector tail test at line 316 still judge the fix in isolation, so a fix that inherits the cut tail of the lines it replaces is still returned as `truncated`. A quote that cuts an argument list, object literal or array necessarily ends on a `,` (`const cfg = {\n retries: 1,`), and a fix that reproduces that last quoted line verbatim is exactly the inherited-imbalance case this change exists to stop dropping — the pipeline then clears `improvedCode` at agent-review.stage.ts:1600, publishes a plain comment and raises the bad-fix notice, which is the identical harm as the bracket case, so the ~25% recovery stays partial for the most common cut shape. Compute the reference's stripped tail once alongside `nonLiteralOf(reference)` and skip the two tail checks when the reference's own tail ends with the same operator/comma or dangling connector.

Suggested code:

const referenceNonLiteral =
    reference === undefined ? undefined : nonLiteralOf(reference);

const imbalance = bracketImbalance(nonLiteral);
if (imbalance.mismatched) {
    return true;
}
return (
    imbalance.signature !== null &&
    imbalance.signature !=
        (referenceNonLiteral === undefined
            ? null
            : bracketImbalance(referenceNonLiteral).signature)
);
````

</details>


